.                 * Interpretation of Results:  
.                 * The primary coefficient of interest is the interaction term
>  (c.daughters_nr#1.d_male), 
.                 * which captures whether the effect of daughters on gender at
> titudes differs between 
.                 * men and women. A positive and statistically significant int
> eraction coefficient would 
.                 * indicate that having daughters has a stronger effect on sup
> port for gender equality 
.                 * among men. Statistical significance will be assessed at the
>  10%, 5%, and 1% levels, and 
.                 * z-statistics will be reported. Residual degrees of freedom 
> are not applicable due to the 
.                 * maximum likelihood nature of the logit model.
